# Build context exclusions for the production image.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded: public/ (33 MB of images the site serves) and
# anything inside it. There is no public/.well-known today, but rules here are
# kept path-anchored rather than using a bare `.*`/`**/.*` glob so that adding
# one later (ACME challenges, apple-app-site-association, assetlinks.json)
# cannot silently drop it from the image.

# VCS + CI (no CI workflows are needed inside the image)
.git
.gitignore
.githooks
.github

# Dependencies and build artefacts -- reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image.
# node_modules in particular MUST NOT be copied in: host binaries (sharp,
# @img/sharp-*) are the wrong architecture for an arm64 image.
**/node_modules
.next
dist
dist-ssr
out
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.tanstack
build_output.txt

# Secrets / local environment. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values come from --build-arg;
# a stray .env in the context would otherwise be picked up by `next build`
# and baked into the bundle.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo

# Agent + tooling local state
.claude
.claude-memory.md
.coderabbit.yaml

# Logs
logs
*.log

# Docs and host-side deploy config that the container does not use
README.md
nginx.conf
nginx.dev.conf
ecosystem.config.js
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
